Z||000012||Fiero5||08-30-2001||08:43 PM||||From: "Warren Meyer" &lt;wtm442@mediaone.net&gt;<BR>To: "Steve Kelley" &lt;stevekelley@nhvt.net&gt;<BR>Subject: Re: Spindles car show Sept. 2nd  <P>Steve,<BR>We assumed you were coming again, so we added a Fiero class this year ...<BR>and we even have trophies!  But the trophies you brought last year were really nice.<P>Our web site is <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/spindlescarclub/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/spindlescarclub/</A> <BR>let me know if you have any trouble. I just went there with no problems before sending this e-mail.<P>I also attached the "electronic flyer".<BR>The cost to enter car is $12 this year at the gate.  Too late to pre-register. That includes driver and one passenger and kids under 12 are free. The old flyer on the web site says $10, but we changed that back in<BR>May to $12.  Everything getting more expensive.  Dynamite goodie bag this year - even includes a t-shirt!<P>See you Sunday - its supposed to be a great day.  Gates for participants opens at 7 AM.  But the best time to get to the fairgrounds is between 8 and 8:30.  After 9:00 the line gets really looooooooooong, and about noon we<BR>normally shut off registration because were full.  Expect over 600 cars this year.<P>Warren<P>His "you" in "We assumed you were coming again", means &gt;all&lt; of us Fiero nuts!<BR>Heh, heh<P>------------------<BR>                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Glowing_Fiero9_sig.jpg">          <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000013||Fiero5||09-01-2001||10:54 PM||||Well, it's almost that time.<BR>Time to go to bed and get ready to head out tomm morning to Marshfield MA.<P>See everyone there.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sunburst.jpg.jpg">            <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fiero5||09-03-2001||04:07 PM||||The Spindles show was awesome! The next show some of us New Englanders are going to is:<P>Sept. 8, Seabrook, NH, Twin State Cruisers Car Show for "Toys For Tots" / as<BR>part of the "Venture Bowl 2001", 9am to 3pm, Venture (Formerly Bailey<BR>Corporation) 700 Lafayette Road, (Near Seabrook Nuclear Station) - Dash<BR>Plaques for the first 100 Show Cars. - Trophies, Clowns, Games & Rides for<BR>the Kids, Barbecue, Touch Football, Appearance by the Patriot Cheerleaders,<BR>Live broadcast of the Oldies Station, & MORE... Entrance Donation: $5.00 or<BR>NEW TOY in its original package. - All proceeds to benefit "Toys For Tots" -<BR>Venture Contacts: Stacy Surprenant or Bob Viel (603) 474-6300, email:<BR>ssurprenant@VentureIndustries.com or bviel@VentureIndustries.com<P>Hope to see some of you there.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sunburst.jpg.jpg">            <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||7
Z||000015||Fiero5||09-05-2001||01:32 PM||||Try and bring a new unopened toy if at all possible.<P>Steve||||reg||12
